  "facts": [
    "Obbola Bridge, completed in the harsh winter of 1988, relied on an innovative artificial freezing technique to create a solid work platform for the heavy pile‑driving equipment.",
    "Spanning Österfjärden, Obbola Bridge links the towns of Obbola and Holmsund, forming a vital segment of Sweden’s E12 highway corridor.",
    "The bridge’s construction showcased engineering ingenuity, using ice‑based stabilization to support massive piles in a frozen environment, a rare method in Swedish bridge building."
